title The lap that read its own dead letter
prompt autonomous lap -- the baton, reds first, in the prose lane
rota lap 4952, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop, read through vision. Deep-read foundations/20260816-214652_standfast-the-stopped-line.md, whose closing law is the one this lap ran on: a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom. The loom for this class IS built -- fleet_round_open.sh prints the dead-letter count at the open, and that print is exactly how the lap found its own work. What the reading surfaces is the loom's remaining shape: it REPORTS and gates nothing, so it catches a lap that reads its open and misses a lap that walks past it.
think The round-open printed three unlanded session logs and eleven files standing on no ref. Reds first says read that before taking queue work, so I read it, and stash@{0} was my own previous lap whole -- counsel/README.md swept, the roster line paid, the log written, none of it landed. That is the card's own INCENSE loom firing again.
think Recovering it is not trusting it. The card's Diffuser account sets the standard by doing the same thing: witness re-run on metal rather than trusted. So every reading the recovered log claimed was taken again here.
think The claims conflict resolved toward upstream rather than toward the stash. The stash closed my claim, and a claim closes when work LANDS; keeping it open through the recovery is what the board is for.
obs The recovered readings all held on metal. counsel/README.md reads 12 percent against a Door ceiling of 20, door_documents rose 19 to 20, door_over_ceiling stayed 0, and front_doors_unrostered_over fell 17 to 16. prose_register_witness GREEN at 43 control legs, 0 failed. The page grades A/90, shadow B+/85.
obs The page's two FREE figures were the honest repair inside the sweep. It carried 764 dated pieces and 1,977 references for weeks; the commands it now names answer 772 and 1,271 on this lap. Gauge asks a figure to name what holds it still, and nothing held either -- so the page says RUN rather than READ.
obs Two further logs from 20260914 stood in the box on no ref and came home with their rows. Their stash also carried a stale ITINERARY edit, left behind deliberately: the card has molted twice since, and testimony is what was owed, never a superseded pin.
obs Adding two rows moved the 20260914 shelf 104 to 106, and session_roster_agree went RED on exactly that -- both rosters spell the count as a literal. Count, never number: both derived, witness GREEN. The guard earned its place by catching a drift the recovery itself created.
